80.desc=Optimization weight for preferring in-place rotation over rotation during translation (higher value = robot prefers to rotate in place rather than turning while moving) Range: 0.0 to 1000.0
81.name= ~weight_adapt_factor
81.default= 2.0
81.type= double
81.desc=Some special weights (currently 'weight_obstacle') are repeatedly scaled by this factor in each outer TEB iteration (weight_new: weight_old * factor); Increasing weights iteratively instead of setting a huge value a-priori leads to better numerical conditions of the underlying optimization problem. Range: 1.0 to 100.0
82.name= ~obstacle_cost_exponent
82.default= 1.0
82.type= double
82.desc=Exponent for nonlinear obstacle cost (cost = linear_cost * obstacle_cost_exponent). Set to 1 to disable nonlinear cost (default) Range: 0.01 to 100.0
83.name= ~enable_multithreading
83.default= True
83.type= bool
83.desc=Activate multiple threading for planning multiple trajectories in parallel 
84.name= ~max_number_classes
84.default= 5
84.type= int
84.desc=Specify the maximum number of allowed alternative homotopy classes (limits computational effort) Range: 1 to 100
85.name= ~max_number_plans_in_current_class
85.default= 1
85.type= int
85.desc=Max number of trajectories to try that are in the same homotopy class as the current best trajectory (setting this to 2 or more helps avoid local minima). Must be <= max_number_classes Range: 1 to 10
86.name= ~selection_cost_hysteresis
86.default= 1.0
86.type= double
86.desc=Specify how much trajectory cost must a new candidate have w.r.t. a previously selected trajectory in order to be selected (selection if new_cost < old_cost*factor) Range: 0.0 to 2.0
87.name= ~selection_prefer_initial_plan
87.default= 0.95
87.type= double
87.desc=Specify a cost reduction in the interval (0,1) for the trajectory in the equivalence class of the initial plan.) Range: 0.0 to 1.0
88.name= ~selection_obst_cost_scale
88.default= 2.0
88.type= double
88.desc=Extra scaling of obstacle cost terms just for selecting the 'best' candidate (new_obst_cost: obst_cost*factor) Range: 0.0 to 1000.0
89.name= ~selection_viapoint_cost_scale
89.default= 1.0
89.type= double
89.desc=Extra scaling of via-point cost terms just for selecting the 'best' candidate. (new_viapt_cost: viapt_cost*factor) Range: 0.0 to 100.0
90.name= ~selection_alternative_time_cost
90.default= False
90.type= bool
90.desc=If true, time cost is replaced by the total transition time. 
91.name= ~selection_dropping_probability
91.default= 0.0
91.type= double
91.desc=At each planning cycle, TEBs other than the current 'best' one will be randomly dropped with this probability. Prevents becoming 'fixated' on sub-optimal alternative homotopies. Range: 0.0 to 1.0
92.name= ~switching_blocking_period
92.default= 0.0
92.type= double
92.desc=Specify a time duration in seconds that needs to be expired before a switch to new equivalence class is allowed Range: 0.0 to 60.0
93.name= ~roadmap_graph_no_samples
93.default= 15
93.type= int
93.desc=Specify the number of samples generated for creating the roadmap graph, if simple_exploration is turend off Range: 1 to 100
94.name= ~roadmap_graph_area_width
94.default= 5.0
94.type= double
94.desc=Specify the width of the area in which sampled will be generated between start and goal [m] (the height equals the start-goal distance) Range: 0.1 to 20.0
95.name= ~roadmap_graph_area_length_scale
95.default= 1.0
95.type= double
95.desc=The length of the rectangular region is determined by the distance between start and goal. This parameter further scales the distance such that the geometric center remains equal!) Range: 0.5 to 2.0
96.name= ~h_signature_prescaler
96.default= 1.0
96.type= double
96.desc=Scale number of obstacle value in order to allow huge number of obstacles. Do not choose it extremly low, otherwise obstacles cannot be distinguished from each other (0.2<H<=1) Range: 0.2 to 1.0
97.name= ~h_signature_threshold
97.default= 0.1
97.type= double
97.desc=Two h-signuteres are assumed to be equal, if both the difference of real parts and complex parts are below the specified threshold Range: 0.0 to 1.0
98.name= ~obstacle_heading_threshold
98.default= 0.45
98.type= double
98.desc=Specify the value of the normalized scalar product between obstacle heading and goal heading in order to take them (obstacles) into account for exploration) Range: 0.0 to 1.0
99.name= ~viapoints_all_candidates
99.default= True
99.type= bool
99.desc=If true, all trajectories of different topologies are attached to the set of via-points, otherwise only the trajectory sharing the same one as the initial/global plan is attached (no effect in test_optim_node). 
100.name= ~visualize_hc_graph
100.default= False
100.type= bool
100.desc=Visualize the graph that is created for exploring new homotopy classes 
101.name= ~shrink_horizon_backup
101.default= True
101.type= bool
101.desc=Allows the planner to shrink the horizon temporary (50%) in case of automatically detected issues. 
102.name= ~oscillation_recovery
102.default= True
102.type= bool
102.desc=Try to detect and resolve oscillations between multiple solutions in the same equivalence class (robot frequently switches between left/right/forward/backwards). 
103.name= ~divergence_detection_enable
103.default= False
